The second-generation Avalon grew larger in almost every respect, except wheelbase. It was still based on the stretched Camry platform and was powered by a 3.0-liter [[Toyota MZ engine#1MZ-FE|''1MZ-FE'']] V6 engine equipped with [[VVT-i]], shared with the [[Toyota Camry]], [[Toyota Highlander]], [[Toyota Sienna]], and the [[Lexus ES|Lexus ES300]], making {{convert|210|hp|kW|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|220|lbft|Nm|0|abbr=on}}. of torque and paired to a 4-speed automatic. The coefficient of drag had been reduced to {{Cd|0.28|link=car}}.

